# g35-fu-host: what the engine wiring (s4-wire-desktop, applied by DESKTOP-WIRE-G7) adds beside the lines kept in deferred-g3.md

1. EngineContext: `leases` is now a member (context.ts, `leases?: Pick<Leases, 'beginCall'>`). Where the context is built, after
   `const leases = createLeases(connection, ctx)`, set `ctx.leases = leases` (build the context with `leases` as a late-bound member, or
   assign it right after). registry.ts then runs every page method as a call on its page: the person's input ends it with -32012 and a
   held page refuses a new one. Without it the calls run unleased (what the tests of the other handlers do).

2. PagesHost.lifecycle gains `reportOpenFailure` (createBrowserGuestLifecycle already returns it) and PagesHost.store needs `redactText`
   (the BrowserGuestStateStore has it): the page the wiring passes is the same lifecycle and store object, nothing new to build.

3. registerSession deps gain `traceDirectory: () => join(app.getPath('userData'), 'browser-traces')` (command-toolkit.ts passes the same
   folder to the old trace export today). It serves `performance` start with `saveTrace: true` (see the .rows fragment of this task).

4. Visibility facts: where the facts source is built (`createPageFacts({ source: { background, visible, ... } })`), call `facts.changed(guest)`
   whenever display-tracking reports the page shown or hidden and when a page moves to or from the background. The popup case is done:
   guest-background-pages.ts calls `state.changed(opener, 'popup')`, which bindGuestState turns into facts.changed in engine mode.

5. The scan test (host/browser-engine/secret-precondition.test.mjs) lists the engine methods from the ServerRequest union of
   packages/protocol: a method the wiring or the protocol adds is then registered in that test too (it fails until it is).
